WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.889
JOE: Processing everyday sensory
information can be a problem

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:07.950
for individuals with autism as
they may be oversensitive, known

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:12.450
as ‘hypersensitive’, or under
sensitive, known as ‘hyposensitive’

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:14.870
or even both, at different times.

00:00:15.679 --> 00:00:20.210
These differences in their senses can
affect how they feel, or act and can

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.300
have a profound effect on their lives.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:26.049
BETH: Individuals who have problems
with their vision may, if they are

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:30.490
under sensitive, have poor depth
perception, causing clumsiness or

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:32.140
have peripheral vision problems.

00:00:32.769 --> 00:00:36.710
If they are oversensitive, they may
need to focus on a detail rather than

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:40.019
the whole thing and they may have
trouble being in rooms with bright

00:00:40.019 --> 00:00:44.010
light such as fluorescents, or even
sleeping without complete darkness.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.360
JOE: If an individual has under
sensitivity to sounds, they may not

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:52.980
respond to verbal communication, they
might enjoy crowded noisy rooms or

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:55.569
bang doors and objects for stimulation.

00:00:56.279 --> 00:01:01.280
An oversensitivity to sound can mean
that sounds seem magnified, distorted

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:05.319
or confused and the individuals
can have difficulties concentrating

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:06.970
because they are distracted.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.740
BETH: Every day smells can be
problematic for Individuals who are

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:15.110
under sensitive they cannot tell what
things are, whether they are safe to

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:19.759
drink or eat and they can fail to notice
extreme odours such as body odour.

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:24.620
Those who are oversensitive dislike
strong smelling products like cleaning

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:29.399
products, cat and dogs, and even
perfumes, shampoos and deodorants.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:33.140
They may also dislike the
smells of foods and cooking.

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:38.620
JOE: Some individuals with autism may have
a restricted diet due to taste issues.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:43.220
If under sensitive, they may eat
things that aren’t edible and shouldn’t

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:45.420
be eaten or really spicy food.

00:01:46.109 --> 00:01:50.759
If over sensitive, they might find
most things too strong and overpowering

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:53.070
choosing to only eat bland foods.

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:56.380
GREEN: Problems with touch can
manifest in different ways.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:01.749
Individuals who are under sensitive maybe
having a high pain threshold and be unable

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:03.960
to feel things, such as food in the mouth.

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:08.330
Individuals with over sensitivity
may find textures of certain

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:10.390
foods or clothing intolerable.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:14.150
They may find being touched
painful and have difficulties

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.850
washing or brushing their hair.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:20.950
Each individual with autism has
their own sensory issues and these

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:24.889
can impact greatly on their lives
and the way people perceive them.
